    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "id": "u16.d02.grammar",
      "title": {
        "en": "Past perfect vs past simple",
        "ru": "Past perfect и past simple"
      },
      "rule": {
        "en": "In a story, the past perfect marks the earlier event and the past simple the later one. With \"after/before\" the order is clear, so the past simple is often enough.",
        "ru": "В рассказе past perfect отмечает более раннее событие, past simple — позднее. С \"after/before\" порядок ясен, поэтому часто хватает past simple."
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "earlier → had",
            "ru": "раньше → had"
          },
          "formula": "past perfect + past simple",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "She had cooked dinner before the guests arrived.",
              "ru": "Она приготовила ужин до прихода гостей."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "past-perfect"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "after + past perfect",
            "ru": "after + past perfect"
          },
          "formula": "After + had V3, past simple",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "After they had eaten, they watched a film.",
              "ru": "После еды они посмотрели фильм."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "past-perfect"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "explains why",
            "ru": "объясняет причину"
          },
          "formula": "past simple (…because had V3)",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "He was tired because he had worked all night.",
              "ru": "Он устал, потому что работал всю ночь."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "past-perfect"
        }
      ],
      "pitfalls": [
        {
          "en": "Don't make everything past perfect — only the clearly earlier event needs it.",
          "ru": "Не ставь всё в past perfect — только явно более раннее событие."
        },
        {
          "en": "Simple sequence with \"then\" stays past simple: \"I woke up, then I ran\".",
          "ru": "Простая последовательность с \"then\" — past simple: \"I woke up, then I ran\"."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reading",
      "id": "u16.d02.reading",
      "title": {
        "en": "The reason he was late",
        "ru": "Почему он опоздал"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "u16.d02.reading.b1",
          "en": "When Marco finally arrived at the meeting, everyone was annoyed. But once he had explained what happened, they understood. On the way, he had stopped to help an old woman who had fallen on the ice.",
          "ru": "Когда Марко наконец пришёл на встречу, все были раздражены. Но как только он объяснил, что произошло, все поняли. По дороге он остановился помочь пожилой женщине, которая упала на льду.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u16.d02.reading.b1.wav",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "u16.d02.reading.b2",
          "en": "He had called an ambulance and waited with her until it came. By the time he reached the office, the meeting had already started, but nobody minded any more. He had done the right thing, and that was the reason he was late.",
          "ru": "Он вызвал скорую и ждал с ней, пока та не приехала. К моменту, когда он добрался до офиса, встреча уже началась, но теперь это никого не смущало. Он поступил правильно — вот почему он опоздал.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u16.d02.reading.b2.wav",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
